# Controllers Folder
# 
# Purpose: Handle HTTP requests and responses - the entry point for API routes
# 
# Best Practices:
# - Keep controllers thin - delegate business logic to services
# - Controllers should only handle: request validation, calling services, formatting responses
# - One controller per resource/domain (e.g., poll.controller.ts, response.controller.ts)
# - Use async/await for asynchronous operations
# - Return consistent response formats
# - Handle errors by passing them to error handling middleware
# - Extract request parameters, body, and query in controllers
# 
# Example structure:
# - poll.controller.ts
# - response.controller.ts
# - ai.controller.ts

